{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DOGFOOD CAPTURE + remediation of the close verdict's one unmet criterion.\n\n(1) The close attempt itself proved the actuator in production: the completion-verifier run for THIS ticket began looping (search_files x10 repeats) and the merged guard aborted it at 84 requests / 105 tool calls (distinct_ratio_window=0.5) instead of burning the full 240-request budget — then bounded recovery still delivered a real per-criterion verdict. Log line: 'llm call [completion-verifier] mode=agentic ... aborted a runaway tool-call loop in 290.9s requests=84 tool_calls=105 distinct=88 max_consecutive_repeat=4 distinct_ratio_window=0.5'. Note max_consecutive_repeat=4 — the old adjacent metric would NOT have fired an actuator reliably here; the windowed distinct-ratio did.\n\n(2) The verdict's single unmet criterion was correct: no test drove a healthy run past the previous 239-request flat-landing threshold. Fixed by test_healthy_run_past_flat_landing_threshold_is_never_aborted in tests/unit/test_agent_call_runaway_guard_c827.py — a high-novelty run with request_limit=300 that lands naturally at 251 requests (past 239) without abort. Commit 6103119afa, Gerrit change 1450, awaiting votes. Will re-close once merged."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785981425258402001,"uuid":"8b925502-f6e0-48bd-b727-eb168900da04"}